Implement common Direct3D shader reflection contracts for all callers.

Derive minimum feature level from shader model and the translated D3D9 code
in level-9 DXBC containers. Preserve encoded SFI0 requirement bits instead of
reporting zero. Validate the data consumed and reject a null feature-level
output with E_INVALIDARG. This is shader metadata, not an assertion that a
particular GPU can execute it. No process-name checks or application profiles.

Regression: winrt/tests/shader_reflection.c; independent HLSL fixtures and
Microsoft reference API results for 9_1, 9_3, 10_0, 10_1, 11_0, double,
extended double and minimum-precision requirements.

